"""Chinese/Japanese noun linking and nominalization, at token scale.

Standalone Chinese 的 and Japanese の have moderate negative activations;
when a token also includes the following noun, its response is much larger.
Clause-linking uses are weaker. Other nominalizers have smaller responses.
Han-character compounds get a weak negative background; any Han token
gets an extra negative response immediately after a noun-linking particle.
The only state is the preceding token's text and document label.
