marks an elision or a dash, and on the word "than" after a comparative.

It responds to:
- the single-character ellipsis "…" (and tokens that contain it, e.g. " …", "……"):
  strongest, about 2.2;
- three-dot and two-dot ellipses "..." and ".." (with or without a leading space),
  and the German/Polish low quotation mark „: about 0.7;
- the word "than" (any case, with or without a leading space): about 0.9 after a
  comparative ("more than", "higher than", "better than"), about 0.5 after "less" or
  "greater", and near 0 in the fixed phrases "rather than" and "other than";
- em and en dashes "—" "–" (with or without a leading space): about 0.5.

